            <ArticleTitle>Precordial ST elevation with acute conus branch occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>180-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 70-year-old man developed anterior precordial ST elevation during coronary angiography in the presence of a normal left coronary artery. Injection of a proximally totally occluded right coronary artery caused occlusion of the conus branch. The electrocardiographic findings are shown, and the pathogenesis is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
